[TEST 2.1] JOIN -> skip order by     

===================================================
col_a    col_a    
1     1     
2     2     
3     3     

Query plan:
idx-join (inner join)
    outer: iscan
               class: a node[?]
               index: idx_join_a_upper_col_a term[?]
               cost:  ? card ?
    inner: iscan
               class: b node[?]
               index: idx_join_b_col_a term[?] (covers)
               cost:  ? card ?
    sort:  ? asc
    cost:  ? card ?
Query stmt:
select a.col_a, b.col_a,  upper( cast(a.col_a as varchar)) from tbl_join_a a, tbl_join_b b where  upper( cast(a.col_a as varchar))> cast('?' as varchar) and b.col_a= cast( upper( cast(a.col_a as varchar)) as double) order by ? for orderby_num()<= ?:? 
/* ---> skip ORDER BY */
===================================================
    
[TEST 2.2] JOIN -> skip order by (desc)     

===================================================
col_a    col_a    col_a    col_x    
5     5     5     1     
5     5     5     2     
5     5     5     3     

Query plan:
idx-join (inner join)
    outer: idx-join (inner join)
               outer: iscan
                          class: a node[?]
                          index: idx_join_a_upper_col_a term[?] (desc_index)
                          cost:  ? card ?
               inner: iscan
                          class: b node[?]
                          index: idx_join_b_col_a term[?] (covers)
                          cost:  ? card ?
               cost:  ? card ?
    inner: iscan
               class: c node[?]
               index: idx_join_c_col_a_col_x term[?] (covers)
               cost:  ? card ?
    sort:  ? desc
    cost:  ? card ?
Query stmt:
select a.col_a, b.col_a, c.col_a, c.col_x,  upper( cast(a.col_a as varchar)) from tbl_join_a a, tbl_join_b b, tbl_join_c c where  upper( cast(a.col_a as varchar))> cast('?' as varchar) and b.col_a= cast( upper( cast(a.col_a as varchar)) as double) and b.col_a=c.col_a order by ? desc  for orderby_num()<= ?:? 
/* ---> skip ORDER BY */
